
1. Smart Shopping & Billing System
==================================
Retail Domain
Problem statement:
=================
Develop a menu-based Python application that allows customers to select products, 
enter quantities, calculate the total bill, apply discounts based on the purchase amount, 
and display a formatted receipt.

Menu options
->View available products and prices
-> Purchase a product
-> Calculate shopping bill
-> Apply discount
-> Exit

Example scenario
=================
A customer buys 2 shirts at ₹500 each and 1 bag at ₹800. 
The program calculates the subtotal, checks discount eligibility,
and displays the final amount.

2. Movie Ticket Booking System
===============================
Entertainment Domain
Problem statement
====================
Develop a menu-based Python application that allows users to view movies, 
select a show, choose the number of tickets, calculate the booking cost, 
and determine whether a special offer applies.

Menu options
-> View available movies
-> Select movie and show time
-> Book tickets
-> Calculate ticket bill
-> Exit


Example scenario
A customer books 4 tickets at ₹180 each. If the booking is for 5 or more tickets,
the program applies a 10% discount. It then prints the booking summary.

Logic practice: conditions, arithmetic, logical operators,
quantity validation, and formatted output.


3. Student Performance & Result Analyzer
=======================================
Education Domain
Problem statement
==================
Develop a menu-based Python application that accepts student details and 
subject marks, calculates total and average marks, assigns grades, determines
pass or fail status, and displays a formatted result report.

Menu options
-> Enter student details
-> Enter subject marks
-> Calculate total and average
-> Check grade and result
-> Display report card
-> Exit


Example scenario
==================
A student scores 85, 72, and 91 in three subjects. The program calculates the total 
as 248 and average as 82.67, then assigns a grade according to the defined grading rules.











